WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.750
Locke &amp; Key is here to enchant us with a spooky
house filled with magical keys and a mysterious

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.120
malevolent demon.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.480
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm diving deep into the secrets

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.670
of Key House to explain everything you might
have missed in the first season of Locke and

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.670
Key.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.470
I'll also be revealing the truth about what's
really behind the Black Door;

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.550
the final twist;
and what to expect in Season 2.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.390
There will of course be spoilers, so take
care.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.099
To properly understand the origin of the magical
keys and where the demon Dodge comes from,

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:33.920
we need to take a closer look at the Black
Door deep inside Matheson's sea caves.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.640
What we know from the series so far is that
many years ago on the night of Rendell Locke

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.390
and his friends' graduation, they went to
the caves to investigate a mysterious door

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.510
they'd discovered weeks earlier.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:49.120
After Rendell opened the door, glowing bullets
shot through from the other side and one hit

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.120
Lucas.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.080
Although he seemed fine initially, later that
night Lucas became enraged and demanded the

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.850
others hand over the Omega Key that opens
the Black Door.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:02.350
Lucas was so angry that he killed two of his
friends until Rendell killed him with a hammer.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.810
In the comic book series that the TV show's
based on, the Black Door is a gateway to another

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.610
dimension inhabited by demons that can possess
humans who come into contact with them.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.630
Similar to the whispering keys in Key House,
the Black Door calls and whispers to those

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:20.890
who enter the cave mesmerising them.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.249
Which explains why Rendell was so obsessed
with opening the door and why Kinsey refuses

00:01:25.249 --> 00:01:27.840
to leave the door when she first discovers
it.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.280
Whenever the portal is open, demons are able
to travel across the threshold via glowing

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.299
metal bullets.

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:37.382
As they cross through the door, the demons
are vulnerable and quickly require a human

00:01:37.382 --> 00:01:41.350
host to survive otherwise they die and turn
into Whispering Iron.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.960
Which is especially interesting because Whispering
Iron is also the special metal that Key House's

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.520
magical keys are made from.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.109
Many years after Lucas's death, his girlfriend
Ellie missed him so much she used the Echo

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:57.759
Key to bring an Echo of him back by entering
the Wellhouse with the key and calling his

00:01:57.759 --> 00:01:58.759
name.

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:02.179
What Ellie didn't realise at the time was
that this resurrected the demon who'd taken

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:03.740
over her boyfriend.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.920
Demon-Lucas, however, was trapped for the
time being inside the Wellhouse because the

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.810
rules of the key prevent an Echo from leaving.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.580
In fact in the comics, if the Echo leaves
through the Wellhouse door, it will fade away

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.920
and cease to exist.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.520
However, the Anywhere Key offers an Echo a
way of bypassing this rule and escaping.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:25.230
By the way, the magical properties of the
Wellhouse may also be connected to the portal

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.560
in the sea caves.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.331
In the comics, the Black Door is located right
beneath the Wellhouse, and in the TV show

00:02:31.331 --> 00:02:35.970
each time anyone goes to the Black Door they
have to travel deep into the cave system.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:36.970
"Yeah, we should hurry."

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:38.230
"That is not what you said before."

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.400
"Yeah, it took a lot longer to get down here
than I thought."

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.760
Duncan also tells the family that the well
has been contaminated with saltwater meaning

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.180
that when the sea floods the tunnels in the
caves, the water must reach all the way to

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.489
the Wellhouse.

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:55.379
While he's stuck in the Wellhouse, Demon-Lucas
hatches a plan to find where Rendell is keeping

00:02:55.379 --> 00:03:00.120
the Anywhere Key and uses the Identity Key
to change his appearance to a female form

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.569
called Dodge, which was Ellie's nickname for
Lucas.

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:07.720
Dodge then magically appears and communicates
to Sam Lesser, one of Rendell's students,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.120
via a picture of Key House in Rendell's office.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.150
This moment reminded me of Pennywise coming
to life and talking to the Losers in a book

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.019
of old photos in IT.

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:21.360
In Locke &amp; Key, Sam's attempts to get the
key from Rendell fail, and he ends up killing

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.620
him in the process.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.900
However, when the surviving Locke family moves
into Key House, Dodge is able to restart her

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.840
scheme when Bode wanders into the Wellhouse.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.500
Dodge befriends him, then tricks him into
handing over the Anywhere Key which she promptly

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.140
uses to escape.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.409
Once free, Dodge begins her mission to collect
as many keys as possible.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.450
In particular, she's after the Omega key so
that she can open the Black Door.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.980
And although Dodge's motivation hasn't been
stated explicitly in the TV show, it's likely

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.340
going to be similar to the comics where Dodge
wants to bring over fellow demons to conquer

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.340
our world.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:59.750
After Bode refuses to hand over any more to
her, the very next scene introduces us to

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.530
Gabe, who's later revealed to be another of
Dodge's alter egos that she transforms into

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.959
using the Identity Key.

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:11.590
As soon as Dodge realises Bode will no longer
cooperate, she switches to an even sneakier

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:15.200
strategy of infiltrating the Locke family
by making friends with Kinsey.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.910
This first scene with Gabe has several clues
that already hint he may not really be who

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.519
he appears to be.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:25.880
First of all, he wears a lobster suit as he's
playing the part of a legendary local monster

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.840
that's half lobster half human.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.490
Of course, Gabe is pretty monstrous himself
as in reality he's basically wearing a human

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:36.020
suit as he's a demon playing the part of a
human.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:41.210
Scot also mentions that Gabe is new to Matheson
and the Invisible Man poster on the wall is

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.140
another hint there's a villain hiding in plain
sight.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:49.050
Gabe's suspect nature is also foreshadowed
when he encourages Kinsey to go down to the

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:53.130
sea caves when the rest of the Savini Squad
are reluctant to do so.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:57.600
And after she finds the Black Door for the
first time, he begins to burrow into Kinsey's

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.800
affections, becoming a romantic rival to Scot.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.840
Gabe's sneaking around appears to pay off
big time because when Kinsey suggests dating

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.210
both Scot and Gabe, Scot turns her down, leaving
Gabe in a prime trusted position as Kinsey's

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.990
boyfriend, meaning he'll be able to keep track
of everything the Locke family do in season

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:17.380
2.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.740
After Dodge escapes from the Wellhouse, she
also uses the Identity Key to transform back

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:24.180
into Lucas and stay at Ellie's house.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:27.900
When Ellie eventually turns on him, Lucas
decides to get rid of her.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:32.930
To do that he uses the identity Key first
on himself to transform into Dodge and next

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.889
on Ellie to turn her into a Dodge lookalike.

00:05:35.889 --> 00:05:39.840
The Real Dodge then takes the unconscious
fake Dodge to Key House.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.660
And during the attack with the Crown of Shadows,
she plants fake Dodge's body there so the

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.910
Lockes think they've caught the real Dodge.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:51.130
Tyler, Kinsey and their friends then throw
fake Dodge through the Black Door into the

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:55.730
alternate dimension, without ever realising
the person they've tossed behind the door

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.470
is actually Ellie.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:02.000
It's unclear whether a human being can survive
on the other side of the Black Door, but it

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.020
feels like there's a possible parallel between
the Upside Down in Stranger Things and the

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.750
alternate dimension in Locke &amp; Key which in
the comics is known by the Lovecraftian name

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.050
"The Plains of Leng".

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.460
OK, spoilers for Stranger Things now.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:19.260
In that show, some characters have been able
to survive their time in the Upside Down.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.990
Nancy Wheeler, for example, crossed over for
just a short moment and was unaffected.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:28.360
However, Will Byers was trapped there for
a much longer period of time and survived,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.660
though he suffered from PTSD and became infected
by the Shadow Monster.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:38.050
In the Locke &amp; Key comics, the demon Dodge
describes its world as extremely unforgiving

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:41.879
and it seems unlikely a human could survive
in such a place.

00:06:41.879 --> 00:06:46.290
However, the TV show has already made numerous
changes to the source material, so we'll have

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.810
to wait and see.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:52.970
For Season 2, we'll also be getting a new
second villain in the form of mean girl Eden,

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:57.099
who was infected by a demon when one of the
glowing bullets hit her as it came through

00:06:57.099 --> 00:06:58.250
the Black Door.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.949
As also happened years previously with Ellie's
boyfriend Lucas, Eden suffered no immediately

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:07.130
obvious ill effects and none of the other
characters noticed what happened at the time,

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.650
so thus far the event has gone unnoticed.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:14.890
However, in the very final scene of season
1, we see Eden working her way through an

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:19.330
enormous spread, just like Dodge did after
she emerged from the Wellhouse.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:24.289
The one character who is aware what Eden is
hiding is Dodge who we see meet up with her

00:07:24.289 --> 00:07:25.800
in the form of Gabe.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:30.879
Speaking of Eden and Gabe, it's intriguing
that both their names have Biblical connections;

00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:34.909
Eden being the paradise Adam and Eve were
expelled from after they were corrupted by

00:07:34.909 --> 00:07:38.280
the serpent;
and Gabe being a short form of Gabriel, an

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.349
angel who was usually a divine messenger who
brought good news.

00:07:42.349 --> 00:07:47.000
Although Eden and Gabe's demonic natures may
seem to be at odds with their heavenly names,

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:51.340
it's actually strangely fitting as the idea
of their characters is that they're not what

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:56.250
they appear to be on the surface as they're
really demons hiding out as humans.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.990
The secondary villain from season 1 that Eden
will be replacing is Sam Lesser whose physical

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:05.740
body died when the Ghost Key separated his
spirit from his body and the door was then

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:06.740
closed.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:11.419
In the comics, Sam's ghost continues to play
a part in the story and I expect he will return

00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:15.960
nex t season in his spirit form and may work
against Dodge now that she's revealed she

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.490
never thought he was special at all.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:22.551
With his mother Ellie missing, Rufus has been
taken in by his uncle in Nebraska, but we

00:08:22.551 --> 00:08:27.370
do see Bode writing to him at the end and
promising to use the Anywhere Key to come

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.370
find him.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.070
In the comics, Rufus plays a crucial role
in eventually defeating Dodge and I think

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.580
his close friendship with Bode means we'll
hopefully see him return.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.951
So what did you think of the first season
of Locke &amp; Key?

00:08:37.951 --> 00:08:41.050
And do you have any theories for Season 2?

